  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 589a77387c7c4ea488d9368fe6c3cd2f, type: 3}
  m_Name: Dialogue 2
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  characterName: Axion
  dialogues:
  - Here you can see the complete production line of the TRANSFORMER.
  - In general, the TRANSFORMER takes a sequence of resources (also known as TOKENS),
    which it then represents in an abstract way called an EMBEDDING. The EMBEDDING
    tries to encapsulate as much of the semantic meaning of a TOKEN as possible.
  - This EMBEDDING is then passed through some very clever mechanisms called ATTENTION
    to add additional contextual information to the EMBEDDING. The result of the
    ATTENTION mechanism is then compared to the contexual EMBEDDING of the possible
    products (our output TOKENS).
  - Finally, this comparison is used to determine which possible output TOKEN is
    expected to be produced. Though this is a probabilistic output, with enough training
    the TRANSFORMER can guess the correct output TOKEN in a plethora of new and unknown
    cases.
  - Pfew...
  - Don't worry! I know it can seem like a lot, but we'll guide you through each
    part step-by-step.
